#!/usr/bin/env python3
# fatigue-brief -- every sentence the user reads about muscle fatigue.
#
# WHAT THIS IS (worklog 2026-09-26-muscle-fatigue-function-tracking, phase 2;
# spec files/outbox/muscle-fatigue-spec.md A3b). The kit computes fatigue
# (kit_life 056, muscle_fatigue.py: muscle-state / muscle-week); this tool is
# the ONLY place it turns into words, a photo and choices. Same shape as the
# goal interview's `next` tools: the tool decides the move and renders it, the
# model carries it verbatim and records the pick. Nothing here is a prose
# rule the model is asked to keep:
#
#   open    session start: heatmap photo (< 1 s) + up to 4 fatigue lines
#           (most fatigued first, grouped by body flow, each "% + when/what")
#           + ONE recommendation chosen by the kit's graded level:
#             none      nothing to propose (a quiet line at most)
#             light     keep the session, warm those regions up once more --
#                       one line, NO question (owner 11:27)
#             moderate  ONE swap package, or care choices when the prior two
#                       training days still load today's planned areas
#             heavy     cardio / small muscle / mobility recommendation
#                       with the regular session one tap away
#           Every proposal carries a keep-as-is choice (11:29) and the full list is
#           one tap away (a see-all button, 11:30). There is NO skip / rest
#           move -- the level table has no such row and the copy gate refuses
#           the words (owner 11:27, 08-23 soft-cost rule).
#   pick    records the answer to `open` (swap | keep | cardio:<method> |
#           small | mobility | expand). A care pick tags this session outside
#           the rotation, leaving its planned day next. Legacy routine picks
#           are accepted for previously saved brief state.
#   slot    at exercise entry: is this planned exercise swapped? -> the
#           exercise to log, one line, and the one-tap way back to the original.
#   revert  that tap.
#   close   session end: 2 lines, no question (+ one draft-map confirm for
#           exercises created mid-session, asked once; silence = kept).
#           session-closeout calls close_tail() itself after its card.
#   retro   weekly retro section (kit retro-sections provider): at most 3
#           lines, facts-only in the weekly card; standalone allows one
#           decision. The functional check speaks only for
#           a user who set a function direction.
#   signal  "my hamstrings feel stiff": write the body signal through the kit and say the
#           module-term confirmation. Pain is not handled here (pain-triage).
#
# NUMBERS. Every % and every time the user sees is a kit output: pct from
# muscle-state display items / node rows, ETA from the node's eta. This file
# computes no fatigue number; it only picks, orders and phrases them. The
# photo carries the same rows as the text.
#
# LANES (D10). LLM lane: turning "hamstrings feel stiff" into --site/--sensation, relaying
# output. RULE lane: everything else (which lines, which level move, which
# substitutes, which routine, every sentence).
#
# Usage
#   fatigue-brief open   (--session N | --day CODE) [--day CODE] [--at T]
#                        [--photo PATH | --no-photo] [--json]
#   fatigue-brief pick   --session N --pick swap|keep|expand|cardio:<method>|small|mobility
#   fatigue-brief slot   --session N --exercise NAME [--json]
#   fatigue-brief revert --session N --exercise NAME
#   fatigue-brief close  --session N [--at T] [--json]
#   fatigue-brief retro  --lane daily|weekly [--mode line|section]
#                        [--week YYYY-Www] [--today YYYY-MM-DD] [--facts-only]
#   fatigue-brief signal --site NODE --sensation stiff|tight|sore
#                        [--side L|R|both] [--exercise NAME]
#   common: --db PATH --program PATH --state-dir DIR
#   env: KIT_DB_DIR (kit read model dir, default <root>/database),
#        KIT_LIFE_SH (kit writes), RENDER_PYTHON (heatmap interpreter)
#
# Exit: 0 printed, 1 usage/env error, 2 refused (named on stderr),
#       3 nothing to say (retro provider contract), 4 routed elsewhere (pain).
#
# stdlib only (the photo is optional: numpy + Pillow, possibly in another
# interpreter). User-facing Korean lives in fatigue_copy.json only.

